## Colour values

The palette in ui/theme/themes/one.json is data, not code, and its own terms
sit beside it in ui/theme/themes/LICENSE.

The Oklab conversion in ui/theme/src/lib.rs uses the reference constants Björn
Ottosson publishes with "A perceptual color space for image processing"
(https://bottosson.github.io/posts/oklab/). They are cited at the point they
are used; the entry is here to record where they came from.

## Linked under the LGPL

gpui's Wayland backend binds KDE's org_kde_kwin_blur protocol, so the Linux
binaries link Rust bindings that wayland-protocols-plasma generates from KDE
Plasma's protocol definitions. Seventeen of those definitions are
LGPL-2.1-or-later, and the crate ships their text at
plasma-wayland-protocols/COPYING.LIB. bviz takes them under LGPL-3.0-only,
which "or later" permits and which Apache-2.0 is compatible with.

wayland-protocols-plasma 0.3.12 — GNU Lesser General Public License v3.0 only
    https://crates.io/crates/wayland-protocols-plasma/0.3.12

Whoever redistributes a Linux binary owes what LGPL-3.0 section 4 asks of a
work that links the library. Of the two things section 4(d)(0) asks for, the
library's complete source is the release above, and the binary can be relinked
against a modified version of it by rebuilding bviz from its source at
https://github.com/yume-ag/bviz, at the commit named in the SOURCE file of the
release archive, with that version in place.

